# Windows batch files keep CRLF in every checkout, whichever git writes them. cmd.exe's label search
# is unreliable in LF-only files: on 2026-09-22 the first `call :pair` in meshroom-pair.cmd failed with
# "The system cannot find the batch label specified" after WSL git (no autocrlf) reset this shared
# checkout and rewrote the file with LF, and DepthMap went unpaired on every card.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Scripts that run on Linux keep LF, so a copy taken from a Windows checkout runs as it is.
*.sh text eol=lf
